openmediavault-spindown (8.0.0) stable; urgency=low

  * First release: spin down idle hard disks that ignore the standby
    timer openmediavault sets, using the same spindown time from
    Storage > Disks. Activity is read from kernel counters and the
    standby command skips sleeping disks, so no disk is ever woken.
  * Storage > Spin down lists the hard disks: select one, click Edit and
    choose how long it may sit idle. The list shows whether each disk is
    asleep or in use, how soon it will sleep and when it last slept.

